e\nEmergency Medicine\nRadiology\nSocial Work\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nPrevious Slide\nNext Slide\nExceptional Emergency and Specialty Pet Care Close to Home\nMedVet Northern Utah is a premier animal emergency and specialty hospital in the Greater Salt Lake City area. Our highly trained team serves as an extension of your family veterinarian’s care.\nServing thousands of patients a year, our team is the trusted choice for family veterinarians and pet lovers. We know pets are an important part of your family, and we strive to provide exceptional care while showing you and your pet compassion. Our team has the expertise to skillfully deal with any pet emergency and provide advanced specialty care for your pet with the goal of getting your pet home to you in the best health.\nIf your pet is facing an emergency, you can come directly to our hospital – no appointment is needed. Our expert team is available for pet emergencies 24 hours a day, 365 days a year.\nMedVet Northern Utah Caregivers\nSearch by Name\nFilter by Specialty\nAll Specialties\nEmergency Medicine\nRadiology\nSurgery\nOur Hospital Leaders\nLeilani Ireland, DVM, MS, MBA, DACVECC\nMedical Director\nAmanda Hemp\nHospital Director\nOur Doctors\nCheyenne Chen\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nHolly Dougherty\n, DVM\nAngela Gorney\n, DVM, DACVR\nRadiology\nRachel Hau\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nBethany Massey\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nAmanda Saulnier-Boyd\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nHailey Slone\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nJesse Terry\n, DVM, MS, DACVS (Small Animal)\nSurgery\nPeter J. Welsh\n, DVM, MS, DACVS (Small Animal)\nSurgery\nPet Stories\n“\nI took my 5-month-old puppy to MedVet and they were wonderful. I appreciated the kindness and professionalism from the staff. They explained delays, offered blankets and water, even dimmed lights so I could nap during my wait. They answered questions and treated my puppy with respect. Highly recommend!”\nPrevious Story\nNext Story\nFinancing Options\nWe understand that planning for the cost of care is important. Special financing and payment arrangements are available for qualified pet owners through an independent company, CareCredit.\nLearn More\nFind a location\nEmergency Care\nFind Care\nFind a Location\nFind A Doctor\nResources\nPet Care Resources\nClinical Studies\nAbout\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nOur Founders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFAQs\nContact Us\nFor Veterinarians\nClinical Studies\nContinuing Education\nCareers\nMedVet Open Positions at New Hospitals\nMedVet Training Programs\nSpecialties\nSpecialties Overview\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nAvian & Exotics\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nEmergency Medicine\nIntegrative Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabilitation\nSports Medicine\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nSocial\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nFacebook\nYouTube\nPartners\nVetRad\nVeterinary Eye Institute\nMedVet Suppliers\nLegal\nPrivacy Policy\nCA Privacy\nYour Privacy Choices\nTerms\nTransparency in Coverage\nTax Information",
